{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.EmSpectralCompleteness","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Archimedean.EmSpectralCompleteness","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Polynomial.Laurent","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Matrix.Basic","lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.EmCouplingProjection"],"declarations":14,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.em_spectral_completeness","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.em_spectral_completeness","kind":"theorem","line":95,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/EmSpectralCompleteness.lean#L95-L149","doc":"**Theorem (two-strand spectral completeness).**\n\nThe endomorphism algebra `End(A ⊗ A)` of the rank-2 block is\nmodelled as `M₂(R) = Matrix (Fin 2) (Fin 2) R`, with the braiding\ndiagonal in its eigenbasis (`diagonal ![λ₊, λ₋]`).  Its two\nresolvent projections\n\n  `p₊ = (λ₊−λ₋)⁻¹ · (c − λ₋·1)`,   `p₋ = (λ₊−λ₋)⁻¹ · (λ₊·1 − c)`\n\nare two non-zero idempotents with `p₊ + p₋ = 1` and `p₊·p₋ = 0`\n(each equals a coordinate projection `diagonal ![1,0]` /\n`diagonal ![0,1]`).  The construction is well-defined precisely\nbecause `λ₊ − λ₋` is a unit (`eigenvalues_distinct`) — this is\nwhere the spectral content enters (`(λ₊−λ₋)⁻¹·(λ₊−λ₋) = 1`).\n\n**Correction (was a false axiom).**  This was previously an `axiom`\nasserting the idempotents live in the base ring `S.R`.  That\nstatement is *false*: an integral domain such as `ℝ` (a valid\n`SpectralRing`) has no non-trivial idempotent splitting of `1`\n(`p₊·p₋ = 0` forces `p₊ = 0 ∨ p₋ = 0`).  The idempotents live in\n`End(A⊗A) = M₂(R)`, not in `R`.  Requires `Nontrivial R` (over the\nzero ring `p₊ = 0`). ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:thm:em-spectral-completeness","label":"thm:em-spectral-completeness","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/em-spectral-completeness.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SpectralRing.hecke_minimal_polynomial_splits","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SpectralRing.hecke_minimal_polynomial_splits","kind":"theorem","line":84,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/EmSpectralCompleteness.lean#L84-L91","doc":"The minimal polynomial of the categorical braiding factors\nover `R` into linear factors with distinct unit roots. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SpectralRing.eigenvalues_distinct","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SpectralRing.eigenvalues_distinct","kind":"theorem","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/EmSpectralCompleteness.lean#L55-L82","doc":"The two eigenvalues of the categorical braiding are distinct:\n`λ₊ − λ₋ = qHalf + qHalf⁻¹` is a unit in `R`.\n\nProof: `(qHalf + qHalf⁻¹)(qHalf − qHalf⁻¹) = qHalf² − qHalf⁻² =\nq − q⁻¹`, a unit by the `SpectralRing.qDiff_unit` field\n(`qHalf² = q` via `qHalf_sq`; `qHalf⁻² = q⁻¹` as units); a factor\nof a unit is a unit (`isUnit_of_mul_isUnit_left`).  Previously an\n`axiom` citing Jones 1987; the unit algebra discharges it from the\n`SpectralRing` fields directly. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SpectralRing.lambdaMinus","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SpectralRing.lambdaMinus","kind":"def","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/EmSpectralCompleteness.lean#L53-L53","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SpectralRing.lambdaPlus","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SpectralRing.lambdaPlus","kind":"def","line":51,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/EmSpectralCompleteness.lean#L51-L52","doc":"The two eigenvalues of the braiding on `A ⊗ A`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SpectralRing.instCommRingR","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SpectralRing.instCommRingR","kind":"instance","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/EmSpectralCompleteness.lean#L49-L49","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SpectralRing.qDiff_unit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SpectralRing.qDiff_unit","kind":"theorem","line":43,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/EmSpectralCompleteness.lean#L43-L43","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SpectralRing.qHalf_sq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SpectralRing.qHalf_sq","kind":"theorem","line":42,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/EmSpectralCompleteness.lean#L42-L42","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SpectralRing.qHalf","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SpectralRing.qHalf","kind":"def","line":41,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/EmSpectralCompleteness.lean#L41-L41","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SpectralRing.q","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SpectralRing.q","kind":"def","line":40,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/EmSpectralCompleteness.lean#L40-L40","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SpectralRing.comm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SpectralRing.comm","kind":"def","line":39,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/EmSpectralCompleteness.lean#L39-L39","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SpectralRing.R","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SpectralRing.R","kind":"def","line":38,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/EmSpectralCompleteness.lean#L38-L38","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SpectralRing.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SpectralRing.mk","kind":"ctor","line":37,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/EmSpectralCompleteness.lean#L37-L37","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SpectralRing","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SpectralRing","kind":"structure","line":32,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/EmSpectralCompleteness.lean#L32-L43","doc":"Ground ring `R = ℤ[q^{±1/2}, (q - q⁻¹)⁻¹]`.  We model it\nabstractly: any commutative ring with `q` invertible and\n`q - q⁻¹` invertible suffices for the algebraic content of the\ntheorem.  In Mathlib terms this is `LaurentPolynomial ℤ` localised\nat `q^{1/2}` and `(q - q⁻¹)`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}